WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:08.966
The TrustLedger live demo runs the real scanner on a sample app. Here: an Express route and a repository in another file.

2
00:00:08.966 --> 00:00:15.973
Scanning the vulnerable version — the same engine that checks pull requests.

3
00:00:15.973 --> 00:00:22.981
The check blocks the merge: a SQL injection, reported at the call in the route that hands the email to the repository.

4
00:00:22.981 --> 00:00:29.993
The trace follows the email from req.query in routes/users.ts into db/users.ts, where it is concatenated into SQL.

5
00:00:29.993 --> 00:00:36.999
The fix uses a parameterised query. Rescanning…

6
00:00:36.999 --> 00:00:44.017
No finding: the check passes and the merge is unblocked.
